# Unit tests for bacapp.c (ASHRAE 135 clause 20.2).  Run: python3 run_vectors.py tests.vec
#
# Expected values were derived by hand from clause 20.2; the digests for long
# values (first 16 bytes..fnv1a64/len) were computed with an independent Python
# model of the encoding, not by running bacapp.c.
#
# Policy decisions exercised here (the header leaves them open):
#  - encoders emit the canonical (shortest) form and reject out-of-domain input
#    without touching the buffer (ERR, never ERR DIRTY / OVERRUN)
#  - decoders accept unambiguous non-shortest forms if the value fits,
#    and reject malformed / out-of-domain encodings
#  - Double and reserved application tags are rejected by bac_dec_app

# ======================================================================
# Null / Boolean (20.2.2, 20.2.3)
# ======================================================================

### null-cap
enc_null @0
enc_null @1
---
ERR
OK 00

### bool-false-true
enc_bool 0
enc_bool 1
---
OK 10
OK 11

### bool-cap
enc_bool 1 @0
enc_bool 0 @1
---
ERR
OK 10

